infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two approximations of "nearest edge"
  desc Anycast vs GeoDNS — what each one actually routes by
  compares
    - label Anycast
      children
        - label Routes by BGP AS-path length (hop count)
        - label No special DNS — standard BGP forwarding
        - label POP change converges in seconds to minutes
        - label Absorbs DDoS across every POP on the IP
        - label Hop-nearest, not latency-nearest
    - label GeoDNS
      children
        - label Routes by resolving nameserver's IP geolocation
        - label Returns region-specific A records, explicit steering
        - label New steering takes effect within DNS TTL (30–60 s)
        - label Failover by withdrawing a POP's DNS record
        - label Resolver location may not match the user (8.8.8.8 problem)
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
